# Gitignored files copied into a fresh `claude --worktree` checkout.
#
# A worktree is a clean checkout of the branch, so nothing gitignored comes
# along — a worktree session would otherwise start with no local config and
# fail the moment it tried to run the app. Only files that match a pattern AND
# are gitignored are copied; tracked files are never duplicated.
#
# Big directories do NOT belong here (copying .venv per worktree is slow and
# wastes disk) — those are symlinked instead, via worktree.symlinkDirectories
# in .claude/settings.json.
#
# Syntax is .gitignore syntax. See https://code.claude.com/docs/en/worktrees
config/override.yaml
.env
